{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015diqRrrJd6fbiUoMqsbffz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project documents, here's what Anchor **is**, grounded in its own files:\n\n## Anchor â€” Productivity System for J.C. Liechty\n\n- **It's a personal productivity / task-management system** for one user (J.C. Liechty), built on plain markdown files as the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`) â€” no database, no binary formats. Everything lives in a single folder, `C:\\dev\\Anchor`.\n\n- **It ships one primary deliverable: `anchor_gui.py`** â€” a self-contained, stdlib-only Python HTTP server that generates an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reading and writing the markdown files directly. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` (not launched by hand).\n\n- **It manages a task lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” with capture (inbox), domains (academic/commercial/family/writing), priorities, energy levels, due dates, and notes, all editable from the GUI or a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`).\n\n- **A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`)** verifies file integrity, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, walks a synthetic task through every state, and writes dated reports â€” surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Its largest area of active development is the R&D Control Surface**, evolved across four planned/built versions (v2 â†’ v4, each Crucible-planned, Foreman-built, all GREEN and merged to master). The current **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** turns each project's window into a single-screen cockpit where each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) is a status-lit tile that expands an inline panel pairing a cached summary with a real, resizable terminal.\n\n- **The R&D surface orchestrates the \"trio\" workflow** â€” researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build) â€” as durable, isolated, server-side terminal sessions. These run over real Windows **ConPTY** terminals (via the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, optional and lazy), each in its own **git worktree** for isolation, with engine choice (Claude or Gemini), per-session and per-project cached/validated summaries, cost/token/time rollups, and stage handoffs between plan and build.\n\n- **It's branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"**, with a vendored brand mark and xterm.js terminal console.\n\nNet: Anchor started as a markdown-backed personal task dashboard and has grown into a **mission-control cockpit for running AI-agentâ€“driven R&D projects** locally, while staying stdlib-only (one waived native dependency) and fully file-accessible."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bad6f19-15ff-4694-af02-c8cd79c80ace","uuid":"99354095-2058-4331-962b-6c1e60ebd41b","request_id":"req_011Cc1fWCCPWpi2LXJ4AB7rb"}
